;; opt.c pass_bit_facts: a test of one bit, (1 << n) & v read as a truth
;; value, made (v >> n) & 1; and instructions whose operand the ways into
;; their block decide made that operand or a constant -- every integer
;; operation the pass works out, under every kind of fact (a compare with a
;; constant, eqz, a compare of the operand plus a constant, two tests one in
;; the other, two ways that meet, a br_table's cases), and a value a loop
;; changes.  Each function's driver calls it on inputs either side of each
;; constant, its parameter plus a constant, and hashes what comes back; the
;; traps are called alone.  Made by test/gen_way_facts.py, which works out
;; every answer.
;;
